# Line-ending policy for glpnet.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS (2026-07-27): `test/run_all_tests.sh` was checked out with CRLF
# on OLAMNIT after the June rebuild, so bash died before running a single test:
#
#   test/run_all_tests.sh: line 24: $'\r': command not found
#   test/run_all_tests.sh: line 33: syntax error near unexpected token `$'{\r''
#
# The suite reported a failure that had nothing to do with any code change. Shell
# scripts, and anything else consumed by a POSIX interpreter, MUST be LF in the
# working tree regardless of the platform or the user's core.autocrlf setting.

# Default: let git decide for text, but never rewrite what it cannot classify.
* text=auto

# POSIX-interpreted files — LF ALWAYS, on every platform.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf
*.mjs           text eol=lf
*.cjs           text eol=lf

# GLP sources: the REPL reads these directly and the R-2 suite asserts
# byte-equivalence against canonical copies, so a stray CR is a real diff.
*.glp           text eol=lf

# Erlang/Gleam toolchain scripts and escripts.
*.erl           text eol=lf
*.gleam         text eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts keep CRLF — cmd.exe and PowerShell want it.
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf
*.ps1           text eol=crlf

# Binary — never touched.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.zip           binary
*.exe           binary
*.dill          binary
